                "senderName": "NWS Des Moines IA",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 3 at 10:27AM CST until November 7 at 2:00AM CST by NWS Des Moines IA",
                "description": "...The National Weather Service in Des Moines has issued a Flood\nWatch for the following rivers in Iowa...\n\nDes Moines River at Des Moines SE 6th St affecting Marion, Warren\nand Polk Counties.\n\nRaccoon River at Des Moines Fleur Dr affecting Polk County.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Raccoon River at Des Moines Fleur Dr, or from Walnut Creek\nto the Des Moines River.\n\n* WHEN...From Thursday afternoon to late Friday night.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 10:17 AM CST Tuesday the stage was 6.1 feet, and rising.\n- Forecast...Flood stage may be reached Thursday afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 12.0 feet.",
                "instruction": "For the latest stream observations and forecasts refer to\nweather.gov/desmoines/water.\n\nRiver forecasts include observed precipitation plus forecast\nprecipitation over the next 48 hours.",
                "response": "Prepare",
